          "code": "OBTAINRETIREMENTINFO",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775751319889",
          "id": "1775841348393",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775841348399_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.DETERMINESOURCE.$output.source==='NEW_TRANSACTIONS'}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Request Input"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776312814689"
          },
          "code": "PARSEINPUTDETAILS",
          "id": "1775841468657",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775841468665_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Extract asset retirement details from the current user message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nThe user may provide a short command, a pasted email, or a table. Extract every asset to be retired.\n\nSupported table/email patterns:\n- Columns such as Asset Number, Book, Retirement Reason.\n- Shared values in prose or summary, such as \"Retirement Reason: SCRAP\", \"effective retirement reason for all items is SCRAP\", \"Book: OPS CORP\", or \"Retirement Date: 31/03/2007\".\n- If a row omits a value but the same value is provided globally, apply the global value to that row.\n\nRules:\n1. Identify all asset identifiers:\n   - Asset Number -> queryFilter \"P_ASSET_NUMBER\"\n   - Tag Number -> queryFilter \"P_TAG_NUMBER\"\n   - Serial Number -> queryFilter \"P_SERIAL_NUMBER\"\n2. Each identifier value must be a separate row in ParameterList.\n3. Do not combine Asset, Tag, or Serial identifiers into the same row.\n4. Book or BookTypeCode maps to BookTypeCode. Preserve values exactly, for example \"OPS CORP\".\n5. Retirement Reason maps to retirementReason. Preserve values exactly, for example \"SCRAP\".\n6. Retirement Date maps to retirementDate and must be YYYY-MM-DD. Convert DD/MM/YYYY such as 31/03/2007 to 2007-03-31.\n7. Cost Retired maps to costRetired. If not provided, keep it empty.\n8. Preserve identifier values exactly as entered.\n9. Ignore totals, requested by, greetings, signatures, and summary counts. Do not treat \"5\" from Total Assets as an asset.\n10. Return valid JSON only. Do not include markdown or commentary.\n\nReturn only JSON in this structure:\n{\n  \"assetRetirementTransactions\": [\n    {\n      \"BookTypeCode\": \"\",\n      \"ParameterList\": [\n        {\n          \"queryFilter\": \"P_ASSET_NUMBER\",\n          \"parameter\": \"\",\n          \"costRetired\": \"\",\n          \"retirementReason\": \"\",\n          \"retirementDate\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"queryFilter\": \"P_TAG_NUMBER\",\n          \"parameter\": \"\",\n          \"costRetired\": \"\",\n          \"retirementReason\": \"\",\n          \"retirementDate\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"queryFilter\": \"P_SERIAL_NUMBER\",\n          \"parameter\": \"\",\n          \"costRetired\": \"\",\n          \"retirementReason\": \"\",\n          \"retirementDate\": \"\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nFor this kind of input:\nAsset Number   Book     Retirement Reason\n107586         OPS CORP SCRAP\nRetirement Date: 31/03/2007\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"assetRetirementTransactions\": [\n    {\n      \"BookTypeCode\": \"OPS CORP\",\n      \"ParameterList\": [\n        {\n          \"queryFilter\": \"P_ASSET_NUMBER\",\n          \"parameter\": \"107586\",\n          \"costRetired\": \"\",\n          \"retirementReason\": \"SCRAP\",\n          \"retirementDate\": \"2007-03-31\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nAdditional examples that must be parsed correctly:\n- \"Retire asset with Tag Number TAG001\" -> one ParameterList row with queryFilter \"P_TAG_NUMBER\" and parameter \"TAG001\".\n- \"Retire asset with Serial Number SER001\" -> one ParameterList row with queryFilter \"P_SERIAL_NUMBER\" and parameter \"SER001\".\n- \"Retire assets with Tag Number TAG001 and Serial Number SER001\" -> two separate ParameterList rows, one P_TAG_NUMBER and one P_SERIAL_NUMBER."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"assetRetirementTransactions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"BookTypeCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"ParameterList\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"queryFilter\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\",\n                  \"enum\": [\n                    \"P_ASSET_NUMBER\",\n                    \"P_TAG_NUMBER\",\n                    \"P_SERIAL_NUMBER\"\n                  ]\n                },\n                \"parameter\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                },\n                \"costRetired\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                },\n                \"retirementReason\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                },\n               \"retirementDate\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                }\n              },\n              \"required\": [\"queryFilter\", \"parameter\"]\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Store Initial Request"
          },
          "outcomes": {
