                      "id": "1774285646342_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Check {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.DETERMINESOURCE.$output.source}} and extract BookTypeCode and ParameterList from the corresponding outputs. Also add CurrencyCode from {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.$currentItem.CurrencyCode}}. Never treat the source itself as BookTypeCode.\n\nORA_REQUEST_AGENT -> extract BookTypeCode and ParameterList from {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.GETRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.$output}}\n\nIf {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.DETERMINESOURCE.$output.source}} is ERROR, extract BookTypeCode and ParameterList from {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.GETERRORINGESTIONRETIREMENTS.$output}} and {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.GETERRORRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.$output}}\n\nORA_INGESTION_AGENT -> extract BookTypeCode and ParameterList from {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.GETINGESTIONRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.$output}}\n\nNEW_TRANSACTIONS -> extract BookTypeCode and ParameterList from {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.NEWRETIREMENTS.$output}}\n\nIgnore any item where X_MSG_DATA contains \"No Matching data for given Criteria\".\n\nReturn only a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  \"assetRetirements\": [\n    { \"BookTypeCode\": \"<string>\", \"CurrencyCode\": \"<string>\", \"ParameterList\": \"<string>\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n- Output must be a JSON object, not a string.\n- Do not wrap the JSON in quotes.\n- CurrencyCode must come from {{$context.$nodes.PENDINGRETIREMENTTRANSACTIONS.$currentItem.CurrencyCode}}.\n- ParameterList must remain exactly as in the input, preserving valid JSON escaping.\n- No extra keys, no commentary - strictly valid JSON."
